--- !u!114 &4715169068357440784
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1703633305335154932}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d85e0dc8a5f3b3d47bddeb04441c359a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NpcTalk
  npcName: Wren Alder
  nameColor: {r: 0.24313726, g: 0.38431373, b: 0.1882353, a: 1}
  firstVisit:
  - 'Oh! You must be my two new field assistants. I''m Wren Alder. I study motion:
    how things start, stop, and push each other around.'
  - 'East of Alderbrook lie the Shattered Grounds: old ruins full of glowing Motion
    Shards, and machines nobody has worked out.'
  - I've left journal stones in there with my notes. Read them, help each other,
    and bring back anything that looks like a machine part.
  - The market square is just east of here, and Bram's forge is past it, at the start
    of the road out. Check the board in the square if you'd like a goal. Off you
    go!
  partsFound:
  - You've found {parts} machine part(s)! I've laid them out on my table.
  - See how they fit? They pass motion from one piece to the next. Something big
    was built in those ruins.
  - Find the rest and we'll find out what it does.
  idle:
  - 'The road to the ruins starts past Bram''s forge, on the far right. Remember:
    what one of you can''t move, two of you might.'
  - Stuck? My journal stones will offer a tip if you wait a little. No shame in reading
    it!
  bubbleOffset: {x: 0, y: 2.7}
  closeDistance: 3.5
  opensVillageFund: 0
  homecoming:
  - 'You''re back! Look over the forest, east: that light is the Great Shard. Whole
    again!'
  - Do you know what you did out there? You pushed, pulled, balanced and smashed
    your way through. Every bit of it was physics.
  - Forces add up. An impulse becomes momentum. Friction drains it away. Weight is
    mass times gravity. You felt all of it, together.
  - The roads east are still closed, but not for long. For now, rest. Alderbrook
    owes you two everything.
  afterRegion:
  - Every time I look east, the Great Shard is shining. I still can't quite believe
    it.
  - When the roads to the Gravity Divide open, I'll need my two best assistants again.
    Until then, Bram's ledger could use your shards!
  creditsAfterHomecoming: 1
